     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"With mfa_admin deployed, exfiltration cannot be reached. The attacker can still get a long way in: exploit_web gives foothold_web; pivot_internal gives reach_internal because segmented is false; phish_workstation gives stolen_user; auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver; kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. Both exfiltration techniques need admin_db or admin_fileserver. Those need foothold_db or foothold_fileserver, which only come from auth_db or auth_fileserver. Both of those require stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin only comes from dump_dbadmin_dc, which requires admin_dc. admin_dc comes only from escalate_dc, which requires foothold_dc. foothold_dc comes only from auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin and is therefore blocked. So exfiltrated stays false.\"}"
    }
